## 2. .NET Backend Layers

Target feature shape:

```text
backend/
  <ApiProject>/
    Contracts/
    Domain/
    Features/
      Items/
        ItemsEndpoints.cs
        ItemsService.cs
        ItemsQueries.cs
        ItemsCommands.cs
        ItemsContracts.cs
    Infrastructure/
    Common/
```

Dependency direction:

```text
Contracts/Domain -> Queries/Commands -> Services -> Endpoints
```

Rules:

- endpoints own routing, auth policy, binding, response metadata, and result mapping.
- services own business workflows and transaction boundaries.
- queries/commands own database access.
- infrastructure owns provider wiring, persistence, configuration, and external systems.
- endpoint files must not use `DbContext` or save changes directly.
- feature code should use named providers for clock, current user/request context, environment, and logging.
