## 3. Frontend Layers

Target structure:

```text
{{ frontend_dir }}/src/
  app/
  shared/
    api/
    ui/
    lib/
  features/
    <feature>/
      types.ts
      config.ts
      repo.ts
      service.ts
      runtime{% if frontend_stack == 'astro' %}.svelte{% endif %}.ts
      components/
  pages/
```

Dependency direction:

```text
types -> config -> repo -> service -> runtime -> components/pages
```

Layer responsibilities:

- `types.ts`: feature-local value/view types and parse schemas when needed; do not copy backend DTOs by hand when generated or shared API types exist.
- `config.ts`: feature constants, labels, allowed sort/filter modes.
- `repo.ts`: backend API calls for the feature, using `shared/api`.
- `service.ts`: pure business/view transformation logic.
- `runtime*.ts`: client-side state, effects, loading/error orchestration.
- `components/`: UI rendering and user events.
- `pages/`: route composition.

Frontend components should not call `fetch` directly. Use feature repo/service/runtime boundaries.
